## Inventory and minimal future extension

`/mapping` partitions **all 1,631 UTF-8 bytes across the six source inventory leaves into 24 contiguous fragments**. Each fragment has an original JSON pointer, byte interval, exact text, exact existing record/manifest field names, representation classification and unsupported boundary. The checker derives coverage from source bytes, rejects gaps/overlap/drift, and checks names against the existing templates; a reported count alone cannot establish completeness. This mechanical coverage does not independently approve the mapping's prose.

`/binding_design` gives the exact proposed joins; `/future_extension` specifies the minimum separately versioned attempt/evidence sidecar. It would join `record_id`, case/pair/repetition/arm, unique attempt ID, manifest and plan hashes, settings/model identities and complete raw inventories. Each object needs resolvable storage identity, SHA256, byte size, encoding/content type, producer/version, attempt and UTC identity plus independently checked content/existence and verifier evidence. No old envelope, schema version, key or null reason changes here. Real validation, runner/scorer integration and trusted verification would require separately authorized and independently reviewed work.

