The synthetic request serializes the exact source common/question/original bytes and empty documentation/image inventories plus the source candidate arm instruction; its hash joins the old effective-prompt field. This proves a local identity join, not delivery to a model. The synthetic manifest changes only two source fields to explicit synthetic model/settings labels; all actual selections, budgets, quota, repetitions, keys, reader/probes and isolation remain unavailable or unchanged. Usage/cost/scorer/isolation/transcript evidence strings are placeholders with `verification: not_performed` and synthetic URIs, not real objects or substantive results. Response claims remain synthetic and are not compared with any key.

